MID_SE_Dit_Buc_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Dit_Buc_C_001: Dietrich. I understand you are always on the\nlookout for a fight.
MID_SE_Dit_Buc_C_002: And if I am?
MID_SE_Dit_Buc_C_003: I thought I might serve as an opponent. What do you\nsay? Shall we visit the training ground?
MID_SE_Dit_Buc_C_004: I do not play. I seek battle true and pure.
MID_SE_Dit_Buc_C_005: That is acceptable to me. Alright. Let's begin.
MID_SE_Dit_Buc_C_006: Let us see just how well you dance.\nTyaah!
MID_SE_Dit_Buc_C_007: Heh! Your strikes are light but powerful! Still, they\nare nothing! Hrah!
MID_SE_Dit_Buc_C_008: So you mean to put up a fight! I did not expect much\nof you, Demon Bear.
MID_SE_Dit_Buc_C_009: A pleasant diversion. I thank you, yet I wonder...\nWhy seek me as an opponent?
MID_SE_Dit_Buc_C_010: Hm. There was a time in my youth when I thought\ntoo highly of my fighting skills.
MID_SE_Dit_Buc_C_011: Then one day my late lord, Guillermo, showed me\nwhat real strength was...and how little I knew.
MID_SE_Dit_Buc_C_012: Why tell me this?
MID_SE_Dit_Buc_C_013: I thought you might be the same as I was then.\nGreen and out for blood. Nothing but a brash blade.
MID_SE_Dit_Buc_C_014: I had hoped to teach you a lesson as my lord\ntaught me.
MID_SE_Dit_Buc_C_015: A tiresome thought. You expected it to move me?
MID_SE_Dit_Buc_C_016: You misunderstand. Our fight has taught me that\nyou're nothing like I used to be.
MID_SE_Dit_Buc_C_017: Your sword showed me... You are not immature\nlike I was. Your spirit is finely honed.
MID_SE_Dit_Buc_C_018: You serve one lord, and that is battle. I have taken a\nliking to you, Dietrich.
MID_SE_Dit_Buc_C_019: We must fight again some time. And I know you\nwon't hesitate to deliver a killing blow. I accept this.
MID_SE_Dit_Buc_C_020: Do you wish death?
MID_SE_Dit_Buc_C_021: No. I have a reason I must live. So I won't let you\ndeliver that killing blow—not yet.
MID_SE_Dit_Buc_C_022: Interesting. I thought you nothing more than Leda's\nstone-faced servant. You understand much.
MID_SE_Dit_Buc_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Dit_Buc_B_001: Hyah! Hrah! Tyah!
MID_SE_Dit_Buc_B_002: Too many of them... If only I were 10 years younger!
MID_SE_Dit_Buc_B_003: Lord Guillermo... Please forgive me...I fear this\nis where I...
MID_SE_Dit_Buc_B_004: What's this? You once told me you had reason\nto live.
MID_SE_Dit_Buc_B_005: Dietrich! Hah. I'm just getting started!
MID_SE_Dit_Buc_B_006: That mien befits you. And I...I had hoped to taste\nblood this day.
MID_SE_Dit_Buc_B_007: Your fearsome sword may be as bloodthirsty as it\nlikes! Now, we fight!
MID_SE_Dit_Buc_B_008: Thank you for your aid. I am grateful.
MID_SE_Dit_Buc_B_009: I require no thanks. Had I come or not, you would\nstill be standing.
MID_SE_Dit_Buc_B_010: I have faith the Demon Bear, ever unafraid to duel\nme, would not fall.
MID_SE_Dit_Buc_B_011: You are correct, Dietrich. I would not.
MID_SE_Dit_Buc_B_012: I am pleased you understand me so well.
MID_SE_Dit_Buc_B_013: Toe-to-toe, blades in hand... Just once was enough\nto truly know your soul.
MID_SE_Dit_Buc_B_014: I see... In that case, I have one request. Ask me why\nit is I must go on living.
MID_SE_Dit_Buc_B_015: I prefer you understand not just my strength, but\nwhat it is that compels me at my core.
MID_SE_Dit_Buc_B_016: I cannot say I am disinterested. Tell me.
MID_SE_Dit_Buc_B_017: I will never tell milady...
MID_SE_Dit_Buc_B_018: But it's that she has not yet found happiness.
MID_SE_Dit_Buc_B_019: Hmm...
MID_SE_Dit_Buc_B_020: One day, she will. And that is the day...the day\nI dream of. Wait, where are you going?
MID_SE_Dit_Buc_B_021: I understand nothing of this sentiment. Our\nconversation is at an end.
MID_SE_Dit_Buc_B_022: What? Did we not just forge a bond in blood?\nWait! Dietrich!